# Student work
student_work/
my_projects/

# Scratch dirs created by `dsl init <office> <folder>` when it is run
# from inside a checkout — which the docs tell people to do.
#
# This used to be a list of five names, grown one incident at a time.
# The docs name twelve targets, so seven were unignored, including
# `my_brief` -- the folder in the README's own Sixty-seconds
# quickstart, and the one course/SETUP.md says Cowork will create.
# Meanwhile `my_stocks/` was on the list and is named by no document
# at all. A list of names could only ever be as current as the last
# person who remembered to extend it.
#
# The property is "a scratch folder at the repository root", so the
# rule says that. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: an
# unanchored `my_*/` would match any depth and swallow the tracked
# gallery office `dissyslab/gallery/examples/my_first_office/`.
/my_*/

for_instructors/

# Example outputs
examples/**/output/
examples/**/results/

# Office runtime output. Gallery offices write JSONL via jsonl_recorder
# sinks; this output should never be committed even if a developer runs
# `dsl run` from inside the source tree.
dissyslab/gallery/**/*.jsonl
# ...except problems.jsonl in the debate office. That file is fixture
# *input*, not runtime output — the gate role reads it at construction
# time, so it must ship with the package or the office fails to import
# (and the test_compiles[debate] test fails in CI).
!dissyslab/gallery/apps/debate/problems.jsonl

# periodic_brief and similar offices write a markdown artifact to the
# directory dsl was run from. If that happens to be the source tree,
# don't commit it.
/brief.md
/morning_brief.md
/your_brief.md

# When `dsl run` is invoked from the repo root (typical during
# development), gallery offices write their outputs there rather
# than inside dissyslab/gallery/. The /*.jsonl glob is anchored to
# the repo root, so it does NOT match tests/fixtures/*.jsonl or
# any other nested JSONL we legitimately ship.
/*.jsonl

# ...and when enough of them accumulate, the repository root stops
# being readable. `out/` is where they are swept. Nothing in it is
# ever an input, so it can be deleted at any time.
/out/

# periodic_brief now also produces a styled HTML brief, and
# competitor_watch writes a markdown digest of the day.
/brief.html
/competitors.md

# gmail_sink in preview mode (default when GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD is
# unset) appends would-be emails here in the cwd. Don't commit
# users' job-match previews if dsl is run from the source tree.
/outbox.md
dissyslab/gallery/**/outbox.md

# job_hunter's job_html_sink writes a live HTML report. Same rule
# as brief.html — never commit a user's run output.
/matched_jobs.html
dissyslab/gallery/**/matched_jobs.html

# `dsl build` generated runtime code per office. Always regenerable;
# never commit.
dissyslab/gallery/**/build/

# wardrobe_assistant runtime state — tracks which items are clean
# vs worn vs in-laundry. Mutates on every run; commits would record
# personal wear history we don't want in the repo. wardrobe_outfits
# is the per-run jsonl recorder output; same rule.
/wardrobe_state.json
/wardrobe_outfits.jsonl
dissyslab/gallery/**/wardrobe_state.json
dissyslab/gallery/**/wardrobe_outfits.jsonl

# Personal scratch in examples/. Add specific names as Mani / Kamala
# accumulate throwaway smoke-test scripts.
examples/try.py

# Logs
logs/

# Maintainer scratch. `dev/app_test/` is tracked and stays tracked --
# git never un-tracks a file because a later rule ignores it.
#
# There was a `!dev/experiments/specialist_agents/` exception here. It
# could never have worked: once a directory is excluded git does not
# descend into it, so a negation below an excluded directory is inert
# unless the parent is un-ignored too. The path it named has also
# never existed in this repository's history. Removed rather than
# repaired, since it was defending nothing.
dev/

# Internal planning docs (not for public repo)
ACTION_PLAN.md
REFACTOR_PLAN.md
demo/
*.cast
*.gif

# Exception: README-embedded demo GIFs ARE tracked. The images live
# in docs/images/; the docs/*.gif form is kept because a stale copy
# at the old path should stay tracked rather than silently vanish.
!docs/*.gif
!docs/images/*.gif
custom_app-for-nyasha.tar.gz

# Local scratch / private notes (not for PRs)
.local/

build/

# v1.6: codegen chdir means offices write artifacts next to office.md,
# so a gallery office may write brief.html or snapshots/ into its own
# directory.
#
# `gallery/**` rather than `gallery/apps/*`, because the mechanism is
# generic: `dsl run --snapshot-interval` works on any office, and
# gallery/examples/ holds offices too. The *.jsonl rule three screens
# up already reads `gallery/**` -- these two lines were written for
# the folder where the artifact was first seen, and the sibling was
# uncovered for as long as they have existed.
dissyslab/gallery/**/brief.html
dissyslab/gallery/**/snapshots/
# recovery_demo/samples/points.txt is deliberately tracked. Ignoring
# it meant every fresh clone got a demo that printed nothing and
# exited 0 -- the headline checkpoint feature, broken for every new
# user. It is deterministic (seed=42, samples/make_points.py), so it
# is a fixture rather than a build artifact.

# Vendor-sourced market data (Yahoo Finance via yfinance): do NOT commit --
# redistributing a provider's history in a public repo likely violates their
# terms of service, even though the raw daily numbers are facts. Regenerate
# locally with dissyslab/gallery/apps/mac_speed_suite/download_stock_history_from_yf.py
sp100_data/
*_1year.csv
*_10_year.csv
*_stock_data.csv

# stray synthetic report preview (generated during review; safe to delete)
.report_preview_synthetic.html
